        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">For most people, buy the JumpSport 39-inch PRO</strong>: adjustable
            bungees, stable arched legs and a 300 lb rating, with spare parts from the maker. If you
            will rebound daily and want the softest, most tunable bounce, bellicon is the premium
            step up; Leaps & Rebounds gets you a bungee bounce for less; and the BCAN SP3 or Marcy
            ASG-40 put a handle within a tight budget.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before you order, check three things: the weight rating against the heaviest user, the
            ceiling against your height and bounce, and whether you need a bar. Then follow the
            folding instructions exactly and inspect the cords or springs before each session. If
            you are still choosing a main cardio machine,
